      "id": 1,
      "text": "Bloomington was likely named after Bloomington, Illinois, and was established in 1872 when the railroad reached the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bloomington%2C_Nebraska",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Bloomington once served as Franklin County seat, with its courthouse centered in the town square and an original 1870s horse trough nearby.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
        4,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.1011now.com/2023/12/15/more-history-bloomington/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "An old windmill beside the 1870s horse trough once pumped water for the town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.1011now.com/2023/12/15/more-history-bloomington/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A bell salvaged from the old public high school now hangs in Bloomington’s former courthouse square.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.1011now.com/2023/12/15/more-history-bloomington/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The sheriff’s office once occupied a sturdy rock jail building, a relic of early county life.",
